WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.811
The Resistance got a badass, purple-haired
new leader in Star Wars: The Last Jedi, with

00:00:04.811 --> 00:00:08.109
Laura Dern joining the series as Vice Admiral
Amilyn Holdo.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:11.280
We're not going to spoil her role for you
here, but anyone who's seen the film knows

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.680
how important she is—and how stellar Dern
was in the part.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.289
For those wondering where you've seen her
before, here's why Vice Admiral Holdo looks

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:19.539
so familiar.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:21.099
Rambling Rose

00:00:21.099 --> 00:00:25.150
Dern is the daughter of screen veterans Diane
Ladd and Bruce Dern, so she had no trouble

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.689
breaking into the business in the '80s with
movies like Mask, Smooth Talk, Wild at Heart,

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:30.769
and Blue Velvet.

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:34.260
Dern really entered the spotlight, though,
with her starring role as the title character

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.740
in 1991's Rambling Rose.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.469
Starring opposite her mother, she earned widespread
critical admiration—and her first Oscar

00:00:41.469 --> 00:00:42.469
nomination.

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:44.210
Jurassic Park

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:48.239
A year after she broke into the big time,
Dern joined the blockbuster fold by starring

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:52.879
in the big screen adaptation of Michael Crichton's
Jurassic Park as Dr. Ellie Sattler.

00:00:52.879 --> 00:00:57.160
Jurassic Park ended up being a huge box office
success and was also a hit with critics.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.329
The film spawned two sequels, and Dern had
a brief cameo in Jurassic Park III.

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:05.089
Now that the series has been rebooted with
Jurassic World, Dern has hinted that she might

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:08.060
be reprising her old role again sooner than
later.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.000
"She's a tough feminist!"

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.659
"We need her back."

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:13.860
Citizen Ruth

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.890
Dern also starred in Alexander Payne's first
notable feature, Citizen Ruth, as the title

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.240
character, a poor pregnant woman who becomes
a central figure in the national debate about

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.240
abortion.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.850
Dern said she suspected that Payne would be
the next big thing when she signed on to Citizen

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.520
Ruth, and her respect for the director may
be part of why she decided to work with him

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.430
again in his 2017 feature Downsizing, which
arrived in theaters just a week after The

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.850
Last Jedi.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:38.270
October Sky

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:43.470
Dern's last role of the 20th century came
in 1999's October Sky, a bio-pic in which

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:47.460
she played the inspirational science teacher
to a group of children who took to rocketry

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.400
as a way of escaping their mining town.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.430
Her character was an advocate and a source
of strength for the boys throughout, and served

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:56.840
as one of the only likable adults in the movie.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.000
Recount

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.610
In 2008, Dern helped HBO rehash a political
scandal in the TV movie Recount, which followed

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.820
the controversy surrounding the 2000 presidential
election.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.929
In the film, Dern plays Katherine Harris,
then Secretary of State of Florida, where

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:14.480
a recount controversy erupted between candidates
George W. Bush and Al Gore.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.610
Dern earned her second Golden Globe win for
the part and was also nominated for an Emmy,

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.220
a SAG Award, and more.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.650
Dern said she learned a great deal from the
experience of playing such a controversial

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.140
real-life figure, telling the Washington Post:

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:30.430
"Recount taught me a lot because my dad told
me you can never hate the characters you play

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.970
and you have to love your characters…"

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:35.790
"I had to just figure out how to give some
humanity and depth of passion to a person

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.640
that had become a huge stereotype in this
country."

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:39.870
Enlightened

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:43.900
Her next small screen role of note was in
HBO's critically acclaimed dramedy series

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:44.900
Enlightened.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.390
"I will kill you motherf---er."

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.099
On the show, Dern played Amy Jellicoe, a woman
who, after a nervous breakdown, comes back

00:02:52.099 --> 00:02:54.050
to work with a new outlook on life.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:58.349
Dern collected another Golden Globe win and
an Emmy nomination for the show and served

00:02:58.349 --> 00:03:00.470
as both co-creator and star.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.620
However, like many critically acclaimed dramas
in the era of peak TV, Enlightened never found

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.659
a big audience, and the show was canceled
after just two seasons.

00:03:08.659 --> 00:03:11.599
The Fault in Our Stars

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:14.800
In 2014, Dern went back to the mainstream
for the teen-oriented romantic comedy The

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.060
Fault in Our Stars.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:19.800
The movie, based on the John Green novel of
the same name, featured Dern as the mother

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.350
of Shailene Woodley's Hazel Grace Lancaster,
a teenager who falls in love while she deals

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.080
with terminal thyroid cancer.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.660
The film was a critical success and arrived
as a box office smash.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:31.660
Wild

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:35.970
It took Dern over 20 years to earn another
Academy Award nomination after Rambling Rose,

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:39.189
but her nod for 2014's Wild was certainly
well-deserved.

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:43.129
Dern starred in the film as the mother of
Reese Witherspoon's Cheryl Strayed, who flashes

00:03:43.129 --> 00:03:47.159
back to her childhood as she hikes up the
Pacific Crest Trail trying to discover her

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.240
true self.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.810
Not only was her performance celebrated, but
it wouldn't be the last buzzy collaboration

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.189
she'd have with Witherspoon.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:55.189
Big Little Lies

00:03:55.189 --> 00:03:59.950
HBO's latest awards season darling, Big Little
Lies, has earned nods for all of its main

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.689
stars at the Emmys, the Golden Globes, and
more.

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:07.189
In the series, Dern plays Renata Klein, the
uptight nemesis of Reese Witherspoon's Madeline

00:04:07.189 --> 00:04:08.189
McKenzie.

00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:13.030
And Dern walked away with a Golden Globe nomination
and an Emmy win, beating out her co-star Shailene

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.340
Woodley for the latter award.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:18.200
Although Big Little Lies was initially billed
as a limited series, it's been renewed for

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.000
a second season following overwhelming fan
demand.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.190
Thanks for watching!

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.020
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.860
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

